'not_excluded'`, deepEqual fails → fail. Good. But wait — the replacement string `reason: 'excluded'` appears in the copy select.mjs exactly once (line 88). Good.\n\nNote C-2 copies `test, scripts, package.json, contracts` into $t and runs `node --test <t>/test/characterization/stable.test.mjs`. My imports are relative → resolve within $t/test/fixtures/... Good.\n\nNow writing check-frozen-files.mjs.\n\nLet me write it carefully.\n\n```js\n#!/usr/bin/env node\n// Frozen-file check: registered characterization/golden files must keep their exact bytes.\nimport crypto from 'node:crypto'\nimport fs from 'node:fs'\nimport path from 'node:path'\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'\n\nconst HERE = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url))\nconst REPO_ROOT = path.resolve(HERE, '..')\n\nconst MANIFEST = ['test', 'characterization', 'frozen-files.json']\nconst COPY_DIR = 'test/fixtures/characterization/v0.1/'\nconst STABLE = 'test/characterization/stable.test.mjs'\nconst SOURCE_COMMIT = 'f75bb76'\nconst FORBIDDEN_PREFIXES = ['lib/', 'bin/', 'config/']\nconst ALLOWED_PREFIXES = [COPY_DIR, 'contracts/spec/', 'contracts/golden/']\nconst ALLOWED_FILES = [STABLE]\n\nexport function normalizeContent(buffer) {\n  return buffer.toString('latin1').replace(/\\r\\n/g, '\\n')\n}\n\nexport function contentHash(buffer) {\n  return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(normalizeContent(buffer), 'latin1').digest('hex')\n}\n```\n\nNote: `.update(string,'latin1')` re-encodes each char to one byte → exact restore of the post-replace byte sequence. Good.\n\nPath classification:\n\n```js\nfunction classifyPath(raw) {\n  // returns { id, detail } or { path }\n  if (raw.includes('\\\\')) return { id: 'frozen.outside_allowed', detail: raw }\n  if (/^[A-Za-z]:/.test(raw)) return { id: 'frozen.outside_allowed', detail: raw }\n  if (raw.startsWith('/')) return { id: 'frozen.outside_allowed', detail: raw }\n  if (path.posix.isAbsolute(raw)) ...\n  const segments = raw.split('/')\n  if (segments.includes('..')) return { id:'frozen.outside_allowed', detail: raw }\n  const normalized = path.posix.normalize(raw)\n  if (normalized === '.' || normalized === '') return outside\n  if (normalized.startsWith('../')) outside\n  const lower = normalized.toLowerCase()\n  if (FORBIDDEN_PREFIXES.some(p => lower === p.slice(0,-1) || lower.startsWith(p))) return forbidden with normalized\n  if (!isAllowed(normalized)) outside\n  return { path: normalized }\n}\n```\n\nHmm: forbidden check must be before allowed. `lib/select.mjs` → forbidden. What about exactly `lib`? Not needed.\n\nisAllowed:\n```js\nfunction isAllowed(p) {\n  if (p === STABLE) return true\n  return ALLOWED_PREFIXES.some(prefix => p.startsWith(prefix) && p.length > prefix.length)\n}\n```\nCareful: `p.startsWith(COPY_DIR)` and p must be longer. `test/fixtures/characterization/v0.1/README.md` → allowed → then it's an existing unregistered file → unregistered error (from the walk). But B-5 registers it? No, B-5 just adds the file. The manifest doesn't include it, so no outside check. unregistered fires. Good.\n\nNow detail for forbidden: B-4 expects `FAIL frozen.forbidden_path lib/select.mjs` — detail = the path as given. If I normalize `lib/select.mjs` → same. Use normalized for detail (same thing). For `LIB/select.mjs`, normalized keeps case → detail `LIB/select.mjs`. Fine.\n\nManifest parse:\n\n```js\nexport function checkFrozenFiles({ root }) {\n  const errors = []\n  const base = path.resolve(root)\n  const manifestFile = path.join(base, ...MANIFEST)\n  let manifest = null\n  try { manifest = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(manifestFile,'utf8')) } catch {\n    errors.push({ id:'frozen.manifest_missing', detail: 'test/characterization/frozen-files.json' })\n    return { errors }\n  }\n  if (!manifest || typeof manifest !== 'object' || Array.isArray(manifest)) { errors.push({id:'frozen.manifest_schema', detail:'manifest must be a JSON object'}); return {errors} }\n  if (manifest.source_commit !== SOURCE_COMMIT) errors.push({ id:'frozen.manifest_schema', detail:`source_commit must be ${SOURCE_COMMIT}` })\n  if (!Array.isArray(manifest.files)) { errors.push({id:'frozen.manifest_schema', detail:'files must be an array'}); return {errors} }\n  const seen = new Set()\n  const registered = new Set()\n  let count = 0\n  for (const entry of manifest.files) {\n    if (!entry || typeof entry !== 'object' || Array.isArray(entry)) { push schema 'every registered file must be an object'; continue }\n    const rel = entry.path\n    if (typeof rel !== 'string' || rel === '') { schema; continue }\n    if (typeof entry.sha256 !== 'string' || !/^[0-9a-f]{64}$/.test(entry.sha256)) { schema `invalid sha256 for ${rel}`; continue }\n    if (seen.has(rel)) { schema `duplicate path ${rel}`; continue }\n    seen.add(rel)\n    const verdict = classifyPath(rel)\n    if (verdict.id) { errors.push({id: verdict.id, detail: verdict.detail}); continue }\n    registered.add(verdict.path)\n    count += 1\n    const file = path.join(base, ...verdict.path.split('/'))\n    let buffer = null\n    try { buffer = fs.readFileSync(file) } catch { buffer = null }\n    if (buffer === null) { errors.push({id:'frozen.file_missing', detail: verdict.path}); continue }\n    if (contentHash(buffer) !== entry.sha256) errors.push({id:'frozen.hash_mismatch', detail: verdict.path})\n  }\n  // unregistered\n  const copyRoot = path.join(base, ...COPY_DIR.split('/').filter(Boolean))\n  for (const rel of walkFiles(copyRoot)) {\n    if (!registered.has(`${COPY_DIR}${rel}`)) errors.push({ id:'frozen.unregistered', detail: `${COPY_DIR}${rel}` })\n  }\n  if (!registered.has(STABLE)) errors.push({ id:'frozen.unregistered', detail: STABLE })\n  return { errors, count }\n}\n```\n\nWait — count for the ok message: \"(N files)\" = number of registered files. A-2 requires ≥ 8. If I increment only for successfully classified entries, tampered (hash mismatch) still counts. Fine.\n\nHmm: should `count` count entries or successfully-hashed files? Use `manifest.files.length`? For ok case all are fine, same. I'll use count of registered.\n\nwalkFiles returns posix relative paths of files. Careful: `registered` for copy files uses `${COPY_DIR}rel`.\n\nNow: unregistered detail must be posix `test/fixtures/characterization/v0.1/README.md`. COPY_DIR ends with '/', so `${COPY_DIR}${rel}` = correct.\n\nIf copy dir doesn't exist → walkFiles returns [].\n\nCLI:\n```js\nfunction main() {\n  const args = process.argv.slice(2)\n  let root = REPO_ROOT\n  for (let i=0;i<args.length;i+=1) {\n    const flag = args[i]\n    if (flag === '--root') {\n      const value = args[i+1]\n      if (typeof value !== 'string' || value === '') { stderr; exit 2 }\n      root = path.resolve(value); i += 1\n    } else { stderr `unknown argument: ${flag}\\nusage: node scripts/check-frozen-files.mjs [--root <dir>]\\n`; exit 2 }\n  }\n  const { errors, count = 0 } = checkFrozenFiles({ root })\n  if (errors.length === 0) { write `check-frozen-files: ok (${count} files)\\n`; exit 0 }\n  for (const e of errors) write `FAIL ${e.id} ${e.detail}\\n`\n  write `check-frozen-files: FAILED (${errors.length} errors)\\n`; exit 1\n}\n```\n\nB-3 expects exactly \"FAILED (1 errors)\". Yes.\n\nNote B-3: does Add-Content on select.mjs produce only 1 error? unregistered check: file still registered. Yes 1.\n\nCareful: B-3/B-4/B-5 copy `test` and `contracts` — includes `.collab`? no. Fine.\n\nBut wait: B-4 adds entries with sha '0'.repeat(64) for lib/, bin/, config/, scripts/. For `scripts/run-tests.mjs`: forbidden? No, scripts isn't forbidden → outside_allowed. For `config/cliworker.example.json` → forbidden. Total 4 errors exactly (my classify returns one error per entry). Also no other errors since the base manifest is intact in the temp copy. Good: \"FAILED (4 errors)\".\n\nNow, note `frozen.manifest_schema` for source_commit check happens before files check — if source_commit wrong, also continue. Fine.\n\nNow check-defects additions. Let me write the code.\n\n```js\nimport crypto from 'node:crypto'\nimport os from 'node:os'\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process'\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url'\n```\nAlready imports fs, path, fileURLToPath.\n\nAdd:\n```js\nconst COPY_DIR = ['test','fixtures','characterization','v0.1']\nconst REPRO_DIR = ['test','characterization','defects']\nconst CANARY_DIR = ['test','characterization','canary']\nconst RUN_TIMEOUT = 60_000\nconst TAP_REPRO_OK = /^\\s*ok \\d+ - \\[repro\\]/m\nconst TAP_REPRO_NOT_OK = /^\\s*not ok \\d+ - \\[repro\\]/m\nconst REPRO_OPEN = /^test\\(['\"`]\\[repro\\]/\nconst REL_IMPORT = /(\\bfrom\\s*|\\bimport\\s*\\(\\s*|\\bimport\\s+)(['\"])(\\.[^'\"]*)\\2/g\n```\n\nextractReproSection:\n```js\nexport function extractReproSection(source) {\n  const text = String(source ?? '').replace(/\\r\\n/g, '\\n')\n  const lines = text.split('\\n')\n  const blocks = []\n  const errors = []\n  for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i += 1) {\n    if (!REPRO_OPEN.test(lines[i])) continue\n    if (!/\\{\\s*$/.test(lines[i])) { errors.push(`repro block at line ${i + 1} does not open with {`); continue }\n    let end = -1\n    for (let j = i + 1; j < lines.length; j += 1) { if (lines[j] === '})') { end = j; break } }\n    if (end < 0) { errors.push(`repro block at line ${i + 1} has no closing })`); continue }\n    blocks.push(lines.slice(i, end + 1).join('\\n'))\n    i = end\n  }\n  return { blocks, errors }\n}\n```\n\nWait: `REPRO_OPEN.test(lines[i])` with regex without /g → fine.\n\n`reproSha256(source)`:\n```js\nexport function reproSha256(source) {\n  const { blocks, errors } = extractReproSection(source)\n  if (errors.length > 0 || blocks.length === 0) return null\n  return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(blocks.join('\\n'), 'utf8').digest('hex')\n}\n```\n\ncheckRepros:\n\n```js\nexport function checkRepros({ root, defects, nodePath = process.execPath }) {\n  const errors = []\n  const list = Array.isArray(defects) ? defects : []\n  const copyDir = path.join(root, ...COPY_DIR)\n  for (const defect of list) {\n    const id = defect && typeof defect.id === 'string' ? defect.id : '-'\n    const sha = defect && typeof defect.repro_sha256 === 'string' ? defect.repro_sha256 : null\n    if (!sha || !/^[0-9a-f]{64}$/.test(sha)) {\n      errors.push(reproError('defects.repro_sha_missing', id, 'repro_sha256 is missing or not 64 lowercase hex characters'))\n      continue\n    }\n    const reproFile = path.join(root, ...REPRO_DIR, `${id}.test.mjs`)\n    let source = null\n    try { source = fs.readFileSync(reproFile, 'utf8') } catch { source = null }\n    if (source === null) { errors.push(reproError('defects.repro_missing', id, `missing ${posix(path.relative(root, reproFile))}`)); continue }\n    const section = extractReproSection(source)\n    if (section.errors.length > 0) { errors.push(reproError('defects.repro_format', id, section.errors.join('; '))); continue }\n    if (section.blocks.length === 0) { errors.push(reproError('defects.repro_missing', id, 'no [repro] block')); continue }\n    const actual = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(section.blocks.join('\\n'), 'utf8').digest('hex')\n    if (actual !== sha) { errors.push(reproError('defects.repro_changed', id, `sha256 ${actual} != ${sha}`)); continue }\n    const canary = readCanary({ root, id })\n    if (canary.error) { errors.push(reproError(canary.error, id, canary.detail)); continue }\n    // ...\n```\n\nCareful: for `defects.canary_error` on overlay escape we need error id canary_error.\n\nreadCanary returns `{ canary }` or `{ error, detail }`:\n```js\nfunction readCanary({ root, id }) {\n  const dir = path.join(root, ...CANARY_DIR, id)\n  const file = path.join(dir, 'canary.json')\n  let data = null\n  try { data = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8')) } catch { data = null }\n  if (!data || typeof data !== 'object' || Array.isArray(data)) return { error: 'defects.canary_missing', detail: 'canary.json is missing or not a JSON object' }\n  if (data.defect !== id) return { error: 'defects.canary_missing', detail: `canary.json defect ${String(data.defect)} does not match ${id}` }\n  const edits = Array.isArray(data.repro_edits) ? data.repro_edits : []\n  const overlays = []\n  const overlayDir = path.join(dir, 'overlay')\n  for (const rel of walkRelative(overlayDir)) {\n    const verdict = safeRelative(rel)\n    if (!verdict) return { error: 'defects.canary_error', detail: `overlay path escapes the copy: ${rel}` }\n    overlays.push({ rel: verdict, file: path.join(overlayDir, ...rel.split('/')) })\n  }\n  if (edits.length === 0 && overlays.length === 0) return { error: 'defects.canary_missing', detail: 'canary has neither overlay files nor repro_edits' }\n  for (const edit of edits) {\n    if (!edit || typeof edit.find !== 'string' || edit.find === '' || typeof edit.replace !== 'string') return { error: 'defects.canary_error', detail: 'repro_edits entries need find and replace strings' }\n  }\n  return { edits, overlays }\n}\n```\n\nThen edits count check needs the repro source:\n```js\n  for (const edit of canary.edits) {\n    const count = source.split(edit.find).length - 1\n    if (count !== 1) { push canary_error(`${edit.find} occurs ${count} times`); ok=false; break }\n  }\n```\n\nThen run.\n\nBuild run helper:\n\n```js\nfunction runRepro({ root, id, reproFile, source, edits, overlays, nodePath }) {\n  const tmp = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'cliworker-canary-'))\n  try {\n    const copyRoot = path.join(tmp, 'v0.1')\n    copyTree(path.join(root, ...COPY_DIR), copyRoot)\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(copyRoot, 'package.json'), '{\"type\":\"module\"}\\n')\n    for (const overlay of overlays) {\n      const target = path.join(copyRoot, ...overlay.rel.split('/'))\n      fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(target), { recursive: true })\n      fs.copyFileSync(overlay.file, target)\n    }\n    let text = source\n    for (const edit of edits) text = text.replace(edit.find, edit.replace)\n    const baseDir = path.dirname(reproFile)\n    text = text.replace(REL_IMPORT, (match, lead, quote, spec) => `${lead}${quote}${pathToFileURL(path.resolve(baseDir, spec)).href}${quote}`)\n    const reproCopy = path.join(tmp, 'repro.test.mjs')\n    fs.writeFileSync(reproCopy, text)\n    const env = { ...process.env, CLIWORKER_V01_ROOT: copyRoot }\n    delete env.NODE_TEST_CONTEXT\n    const result = spawnSync(nodePath, ['--test', '--test-reporter=tap', '--test-name-pattern=\\\\[repro\\\\]', reproCopy], { cwd: tmp, env, encoding: 'utf8', timeout: RUN_TIMEOUT, maxBuffer: 16*1024*1024 })\n    return { status: result.status, output: `${result.stdout ?? ''}${result.stderr ?? ''}`, error: result.error ?? null }\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(tmp, { recursive: true, force: true })\n  }\n}\n```\n\nNote `text.replace(edit.find, edit.replace)` — `find` is a literal string, fine (no regex). Use split/join to avoid $ patterns in replace: `text.split(edit.find).join(edit.replace)`.\n\nThen baseline:\n```js\n    const baseline = runRepro({ ...no overlays, no edits })\n    if (!(baseline.status === 0 && TAP_REPRO_OK.test(baseline.output) && !TAP_REPRO_NOT_OK.test(baseline.output))) {\n      push baseline_failed\n      continue\n    }\n    const canaryRun = runRepro({...with overlays+edits})\n    if (!TAP_REPRO_NOT_OK.test(canaryRun.output)) push canary_survived `${id} ...`\n```\n\nCareful: `TAP_REPRO_OK` has /m but not /g, so `.test` is stateless. Good.\n\nDetail messages: e.g. `defects.canary_survived a5-dup-call the repro still passes on the canary variant`.\n\nNow `walkRelative(dir)` returns posix relative file paths.\n\ncopyTree: recursive copy.\n\nNow CLI changes:\n\n```js\n  let strict = args includes '--strict'\n  let rootGiven = false\n  ...\n  if (flag === '--strict') strict = true\n  ...\n  const strictMode = strict || !rootGiven\n```\n\nCareful: must add `--strict` to the unknown-arg handler and usage string.\n\nAfter checkDefects:\n```js\n  let errors = [...base.errors]\n  if (strictMode && !base.absent) {\n    const ledger = readLedger(root)\n    if (ledger && Array.isArray(ledger.defects)) {\n      if (!errors.some(e => e.id === 'defects.set_mismatch')) {\n        const actual = ledger.defects.map(d => d && d.id).filter(x => typeof x === 'string').sort()\n        const expected = [...EXPECTED_IDS].sort()\n        if (actual.length !== expected.length || actual.some((id,i)=>id!==expected[i])) {\n          errors.push({ id:'defects.set_mismatch', detail: `ledger ids ${actual.join(',')} != ${expected.join(',')}` })\n        }\n      }\n      errors.push(...checkRepros({ root, defects: ledger.defects, nodePath: process.execPath }))\n    }\n  }\n```\n\nHmm, careful: baseline/canary runs use `process.execPath`. Design says `nodePath` param. Default process.execPath.\n\nWait: an important problem. check-defects is run by check-fast, which runs within `npm test`? No: check-fast runs check-*.mjs first, then run-tests. So check-defects spawns 22 `node --test` processes sequentially. Then npm test runs the full suite which includes repro files (they're .test.mjs with [repro] titles). Fine.\n\nPotential recursion: the repro runs `node --test repro.test.mjs` in tmp. Those repro files don't call check-defects. Fine.\n\nBut: a5-nocache repro spawns node within node --test → nested but no NODE_TEST_CONTEXT (we delete it). Good.\n\nNow, `defects.missing_fixed` for a3-runner in strict mode: a3-runner requires [fixed] section — it has one and AC-001 is covered. Good.\n\nNow — CRITICAL: `required` in checkDefects default mode uses mergeShards, which reports errors for shards. It filters `valid` defects whose ac is 'covered'. With T-002.json covering AC-005, fine.\n\nAnother critical: since the strict run happens on the real repo, checkRepros will run all 11 defects' baseline+canary = 22 subprocesses. Each spawns node --test which... hmm, `node --test` on a single file takes ~150-400ms. Fine.\n\nNow: the a5-nocache repro spawns `node probe.mjs` twice. On win32 with shell:true it's `node probe.mjs` via cmd. Should work.\n\nWait: in the canary variant (cached), 1 spawn.\n\nAnother issue: node --test in the tmp dir with cwd=tmp. The repro calls process.chdir(tmpA) then restores. OK.\n\nNow the canary for a5-shell overlay availability.mjs with `shell: false` — but a5-nocache canary is separate.\n\nNow let me also double check: canary overlay files for a5-unused include cli.mjs — but wait, for the baseline run of a5-unused, the repro reads V01/lib/cli.mjs from the *copied* copy. Yes `<tmp>/v0.1/lib/cli.mjs`.\n\nNow `test/characterization/canary/**` must not contain `*.test.mjs`. Our overlay files: select.mjs, config.mjs, forecast.mjs, availability.mjs, cli.mjs (as `lib/cli.mjs`), etc.\n\nWait — overlay/lib/cli.mjs ends with `.mjs`, not `.test.mjs`. Fine.\n\nNow: `findOrphans` — canary files under test/characterization are not .test.mjs → not orphans.\n\n`enumerateTestFiles` only picks `*.test.mjs` → overlays excluded.\n\nNow: the full run (A-5) will run all repro files as tests, including a5-nocache which spawns node. And a4-paths, a4-null-config which mutate env (CLIWORKER_HOME) — each test file runs in its own process, so no cross-contamination. But within the same file, the repro block mutates process.env.CLIWORKER_HOME with try/finally. Fine.\n\nHmm, but careful: node --test by default runs each *file* in a separate child process. Yes.\n\nNow: full run's repro for a5-nocache does process.chdir — restores. Fine.\n\nNow let me write the defects.json generation script — but I can't create extra files. I'll use `node -e` inline to compute hashes and write defects.json / frozen-files.json. That's allowed (no new persistent files besides target outputs).\n\nOrder of work:\n1. Write check-frozen-files.mjs\n2. Write check-defects.mjs additions\n3. Write 10 repro files\n4. Write canaries (11 dirs, overlays)\n5. Write stable.test.mjs\n6. Generate defects.json + frozen-files.json\n7. Write test/unit/frozen-files.test.mjs\n8. Write test/traceability/T-002.json\n9. Run