{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b6e8-9568-7162-a490-436972a90538","session_id":"01a1b6e5-b62d-77fa-b8d6-e09057b99f7b","message":{"id":"01a1b6e895687162a4904367b29cc15f","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 6 pass. Now write the 10 repro files.\n\nCommon header per file:\n```js\nimport test from 'node:test'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict'\nimport fs from 'node:fs'\nimport os from 'node:os'\nimport path from 'node:path'\nimport { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from 'node:url'\n\nconst V01 = process.env.CLIWORKER_V01_ROOT\n  ?? fileURLToPath(new URL('../../fixtures/characterization/v0.1/', import.meta.url))\n```\n\nCareful: only import what's used to avoid lint issues (no linter here). But E-3 checks imports are only '.' or 'node:'. All node: prefixed → fine.\n\nNote D-3 requires each file contain 'CLIWORKER_V01_ROOT' — yes.\n\nCareful: the file must not contain the string `[fixed]` anywhere. Comments: avoid.\n\nAlso each file must not contain a second `test('[repro]` line at column 0. Only one.\n\nLet me write a1-quota.\n\nAlso careful: `assert.match(source, /regex/)` etc.\n\nFor a1, the assertion \"结果没有 `remaining_fraction`、`risk_basis` 键\".\n\nLet me write each file now.\n\nFile 1: a1-quota.test.mjs\n\n```js\nimport test from 'node:test'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict'\nimport path from 'node:path'\nimport { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from 'node:url'\n\nconst V01 = process.env.CLIWORKER_V01_ROOT\n  ?? fileURLToPath(new URL('../../fixtures/characterization/v0.1/', import.meta.url))\n\ntest('[repro] [AC-005] a percentage quota turns the forecast into unknown', async () => {\n  const { forecast } = await import(pathToFileURL(path.join(V01, 'lib', 'forecast.mjs')).href)\n  const now = Date.UTC(2026, 0, 1, 12, 0, 0)\n  const records = [1, 2, 3].map((i) => ({\n    model: 'claude-quick',\n    at: new Date(now - i * 10 * 60_000).toISOString(),\n    cost_usd: 0.5,\n  }))\n\n  const percent = forecast({ records, model: 'claude-quick', quota: { remaining_pct: 5 }, now })\n  assert.equal(percent.risk, 'unknown')\n  assert.equal(percent.tasks_left, null)\n  assert.equal('remaining_fraction' in percent, false)\n  assert.equal('risk_basis' in percent, false)\n\n  const credits = forecast({ records, model: 'claude-quick', quota: { remaining: 1, unit: 'credits' }, now })\n  assert.equal(credits.risk, 'unknown')\n  assert.equal('reason' in credits, false)\n})\n```\nWait: opening line must end with `{`. `test('...', async () => {` yes.\n\n`assert.equal('remaining_fraction' in percent, false)` — fine.\n\nNow a2-pack:\n\n```js\nimport test from 'node:test'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict'\nimport fs from 'node:fs'\nimport path from 'node:path'\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'\n\nconst V01 = process.env.CLIWORKER_V01_ROOT\n  ?? fileURLToPath(new URL('../../fixtures/characterization/v0.1/', import.meta.url))\n\n// The v0.1 copy carries no package.json on purpose, so its published shape is inlined here.\nconst V01_PACKAGE = { bin: null, files: ['lib', 'cordis.patch.yml', 'dsh.plugin.json', 'README.md'] }\n\ntest('[repro] [AC-005] 0.1 publishes no bin directory and no config directory', () => {\n  assert.equal(V01_PACKAGE.bin, null)\n  assert.equal(V01_PACKAGE.files.includes('bin'), false)\n  assert.equal(V01_PACKAGE.files.includes('config'), false)\n  assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(V01, 'config', 'cliworker.example.json')), true)\n})\n```\nCareful: canary repro_edits find `bin: null` → replace `bin: 'bin/cliworker.mjs'`. In the source, `bin: null` appears in `const V01_PACKAGE = { bin: null, files: ...` — once. Good. But also the phrase appears in... no.\n\nHmm, but the opening line of the test is `test('...', () => {` — ends with `{`. Good. And `})` at column 0.\n\na4-paths:\n\n```js\nimport test from 'node:test'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict'\nimport fs from 'node:fs'\nimport os from 'node:os'\nimport path from 'node:path'\nimport { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from 'node:url'\n\nconst V01 = process.env.CLIWORKER_V01_ROOT\n  ?? fileURLToPath(new URL('../../fixtures/characterization/v0.1/', import.meta.url))\n\ntest('[repro] [AC-005] config home ignores the directory of the config file', async () => {\n  const { loadConfig } = await import(pathToFileURL(path.join(V01, 'lib', 'config.mjs')).href)\n  const base = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'cw-v01-paths-'))\n  const home = path.join(base, 'home')\n  const first = path.join(base, 'first')\n  const second = path.join(base, 'second')\n  const previous = process.env.CLIWORKER_HOME\n  try {\n    for (const dir of [home, first, second]) fs.mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true })\n    const firstFile = path.join(first, 'config.json')\n    const secondFile = path.join(second, 'config.json')\n    for (const file of [firstFile, secondFile]) {\n      fs.writeFileSync(file, JSON.stringify({ providers: {}, models: {} }), 'utf8')\n    }\n    process.env.CLIWORKER_HOME = home\n\n    const a = loadConfig({ file: firstFile })\n    const b = loadConfig({ file: secondFile })\n\n    assert.equal(a._home, b._home)\n    assert.equal(path.resolve(a._home).startsWith(path.resolve(first) + path.sep), false)\n    assert.equal(path.resolve(b._home).startsWith(path.resolve(second) + path.sep), false)\n  } finally {\n    if (previous === undefined) delete process.env.CLIWORKER_HOME\n    else process.env.CLIWORKER_HOME = previous\n    fs.rmSync(base, { recursive: true, force: true })\n  }\n})\n```\nCareful: opening line ends with `{`. And the block contains lines ending with `{` but at column 0? No — nested lines are indented.\n\nCareful: `})` at column 0 — the final `})` of the test. But inside, are there any lines exactly `})` at column 0? No.\n\na4-null-config similar.\n\na5-dup-call: no fs/os needed.\n\na5-forecast-x3: needs Proxy; no fs.\n\na5-unused: fs, path.\n\na5-shell: fs, path.\n\na5-nocache: fs, os, path.\n\na5-ignored-fields: no fs.\n\nNow let me consider the forecast-x3 proxy carefully. `config.quotas` Proxy. `config.quotas?.[m.provider]` — get trap with prop 'claude'. Count 12+.\n\nActually wait: in selectModels, `rank` is called from the comparator — but for 12 items, sort calls comparator multiple times; each comparator call invokes rank(a) and rank(b), each doing a forecast → 2 reads per comparison. So reads = 12 (filter) + 2*comparisons + 12 (picked). Definitely > 12.\n\nBut hold on: is the candidate filter run before rank? Yes, filter first. All 12 pass; then sort; then picked slice(0,12).\n\nAlso `Number(request.count || 1)` = 12 → count = min(10, 12) = 10! Careful: `Math.max(1, Math.min(10, Number(request.count || 1)))` → count = 10 with count:12. So only 10 picked. That's fine — assertions: `result.models.length` would be 10, not 12. Let me not assert 12; assert `>= 10`, or just assert reads > 12.\n\nHmm, better: assert `result.models.length === 10`? That's 0.1-specific but fine as a repro. Actually simpler: assert `result.ok === true` and `reads > 12`. But if count is 10, picked map does 10 reads. Total = 12 + 2*cmp + 10 > 12 anyway. Fine.\n\nFor the canary, memoized per model key: 12 reads total (12 models × 1). assert reads > 12 fails. \n\nWait — careful with canary overlay: I need to modify select.mjs so that `config.quotas?.[m.provider]` is read exactly once per model key. Model keys: claude-m0..m11 → 12 distinct keys → 12 reads. Good.\n\nBut hold on: the memo must also be used for `handle.quota`. Yes.\n\nLet me now write the canary select.mjs files. There are three select.mjs canaries (a5-dup-call, a5-forecast-x3, a5-unused, a5-ignored-fields) — that's four actually. Each is a full copy of the 0.1 select.mjs with one modification. I'll generate them with a script from the copy to avoid manual transcription errors. But I can't create a helper script file... I can use `node -e` with inline code that reads the copy, applies replacements, writes overlay. That works.\n\nLet me plan overlay generation via node -e:\n\n1. a5-dup-call/overlay/lib/select.mjs: re