{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b6e9-4d14-7ca7-a754-f8decea17a36","session_id":"01a1b6e5-b62d-77fa-b8d6-e09057b99f7b","message":{"id":"01a1b6e94d1373679b40951a2a83f1e8","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 11 repros pass. Now build canaries.\n\nOrder: create canary dirs and canary.json, plus overlays.\n\nCanary list:\n1. a1-quota: overlay lib/forecast.mjs (fixed variant)\n2. a2-pack: repro_edits [{find:'bin: null', replace:\"bin: 'bin/cliworker.mjs'\"}]\n3. a3-runner: repro_edits [{find:'scripts: null,', replace:\"scripts: { test: 'node scripts/run-tests.mjs' },\"}]\n4. a4-paths: overlay lib/config.mjs\n5. a4-null-config: overlay lib/config.mjs\n6. a5-dup-call: overlay lib/select.mjs\n7. a5-forecast-x3: overlay lib/select.mjs\n8. a5-unused: overlay lib/select.mjs + lib/cli.mjs\n9. a5-ignored-fields: overlay lib/select.mjs\n10. a5-shell: overlay lib/availability.mjs\n11. a5-nocache: overlay lib/availability.mjs\n\nLet me write overlay files.\n\na1-quota overlay forecast.mjs: full file with remaining_pct support.\n\n```js\nexport const DEFAULT_PRICES = { input_per_mtok: 0, output_per_mtok: 0 }\n\nexport function normalizePrices(m = {}) { ... }\nexport function estimateCost(...) { ... }\n\nexport function forecast({ records = [], model, prices, quota = null, now = Date.now() } = {}) {\n  ...same...\n  let remainingFraction = null\n  if (quota && Number.isFinite(Number(quota.remaining_pct))) remainingFraction = Number(quota.remaining_pct) / 100\n  ...\n  const risk = remainingFraction !== null ? 'low_reserve' : (tasksLeft == null ? 'unknown' : ...)\n  return {\n    status: 'known', ...,\n    remaining_fraction: remainingFraction,\n    risk,\n  }\n}\n```\nCareful: The repro asserts `percent.risk === 'unknown'` first → 'low_reserve' → fails. \n\nAlso for the credits case: risk? remainingFraction null → tasksLeft null → 'unknown'. Fine; it fails earlier anyway.\n\nNote: canary overlay files must be valid ESM.\n\na4-paths overlay config.mjs: `_home: path.join(path.dirname(root), 'state')`.\n\na4-null-config overlay config.mjs:\n```js\nexport function loadConfig({ file } = {}) {\n  const root = path.resolve(...)\n  let raw\n  try { raw = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(root,'utf8')) } catch (e) {\n    const error = new Error(...); error.code = 'E_CONFIG'; throw error\n  }\n  if (!raw || (typeof raw !== 'object')) { const error = new Error('config must be an object'); error.code='E_CONFIG'; throw error }\n  if (raw.schema && raw.schema !== SCHEMA) { const error = new Error(`unsupported...`); error.code='E_CONFIG'; throw error }\n  if (!raw.providers || typeof raw.providers !== 'object') { const error = new Error('providers is required'); error.code='E_CONFIG'; throw error }\n  if (!raw.models || typeof raw.models !== 'object') { ... E_CONFIG }\n  return { ...raw, _file: root, _home: defaultHome() }\n}\n```\nThen repro's first assert `fromNull instanceof TypeError` fails (it's an Error, and code defined). Good → not ok.\n\na4-paths and a4-null-config overlays both are config.mjs with different modifications; separate directories so fine.\n\na5-dup-call overlay select.mjs: 0.1 minus `cli: call`.\na5-forecast-x3 overlay select.mjs: with quota memo.\na5-unused overlay select.mjs: minus isObject; cli.mjs: minus fs import.\na5-ignored-fields overlay select.mjs: with warnings.\na5-shell overlay availability.mjs: shell: false.\na5-nocache overlay availability.mjs: WeakMap cache.\n\nI'll generate select.mjs overlays via node -e from the copy with string replacements (safer than retyping 132 lines).\n\nLet me do it with a single node -e that performs all overlay writes for select/cli/availability, and separately Write the forecast.mjs and config.mjs overlays by hand.\n\nActually I can do all with node -e using replacements on the copy. But readability of generated overlays matters less than correctness. For forecast/config I'd need multi-line replacements — doable but fragile. Let me hand-write config.mjs and forecast.mjs overlays (short files) and node-generate the select.mjs/cli.mjs/availability.mjs ones... availability.mjs is short too (38 lines), hand-write is fine but risk of typos — it's generated from the copy? For shell:false and cache versions, replacements are simple one-liners:\n\n- a5-shell: replace `shell: process.platform === 'win32'` with `shell: false`. Single occurrence.\n- a5-nocache: need caching → structural. Hand-write full file or do replacement:\n  - insert `const CACHE = new WeakMap()` after import line\n  - add cache lookup/insert into checkProvider.\n\nDoing this via targeted replacements is tricky. I'll hand-write a5-nocache's availability.mjs fully — it's ~40 lines, manageable.\n\nLet me write the files. First config.mjs overlays and forecast.mjs overlay.\n\nFor a4-paths overlay config.mjs — full copy with `_home` change:\n\n```js\nimport fs from 'node:fs'\nimport os from 'node:os'\nimport path from 'node:path'\n\nexport const SCHEMA = 'cliworker.config/v1'\n\nexport function defaultHome() {\n  return process.env.CLIWORKER_HOME || path.join(os.homedir(), '.cliworker')\n}\n\nexport function loadConfig({ file } = {}) {\n  const root = path.resolve(file || process.env.CLIWORKER_CONFIG || path.join(defaultHome(), 'config.json'))\n  let raw\n  try { raw = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(root, 'utf8')) } catch (e) {\n    const error = new Error(`cannot read CLIWorker config ${root}: ${e.message}`)\n    error.code = 'E_CONFIG'\n    throw error\n  }\n  if (!raw || raw.schema && raw.schema !== SCHEMA) throw new Error(`unsupported CLIWorker config schema: ${raw.schema}`)\n  if (!raw.providers || typeof raw.providers !== 'object') throw new Error('providers is required')\n  if (!raw.models || typeof raw.models !== 'object') throw new Error('models is required')\n  return { ...raw, _file: root, _home: path.join(path.dirname(root), 'state') }\n}\n```\nHmm — careful: a4-paths repro asserts `a._home` !== first-dir-based... wait it asserts NOT startsWith(dirA). With `_home = dirname(root)/state` = first/state → startsWith(first) → assertion `false` fails. Good.\n\nBut: does a4-paths canary accidentally also fix a4-null-config? No, independent dirs.\n\nNote: `readUsage`/`appendUsage` not needed for the overlay but keeping the file complete is fine. I'll keep them.\n\nFor a4-null-config overlay: config.mjs with E_CONFIG codes.\n\nNow write.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6e5ba867444bd771672006700a3","_messageId":"01a1b6e94d1373679b40951a2a83f1e8","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b6e5ba867444bd771672006700a3","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6e94d1373679b40951a2a83f1e8","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6e94d1373679b40951a2a83f1e8","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b6e9-4d14-7ca7-a754-f8decea17a36","traceparent":"00-4a75c094774db18b4fa9b0e599d0db42-f8dbe608f8e504b0-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b6e5-b62d-77fa-b8d6-e09057b99f7b,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b6e5ba867444bd771672006700a3"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T16:48:37.318Z"}
