{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b6e9-954a-7cd5-917d-7c20fa30ec9b","session_id":"01a1b6e5-b62d-77fa-b8d6-e09057b99f7b","message":{"id":"01a1b6e995497f3fbd0be5ac13c7caef","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now a5-nocache overlay availability.mjs with caching keyed on provider object.\n\n```js\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process'\n\nconst STATUS_CACHE = new WeakMap()\n\nfunction run(...) {...}\n\nexport function checkProvider(provider, { probe = true } = {}) {\n  const cli = provider.cli\n  if (!probe) return { state: 'unverified', version: null, detail: 'probe disabled' }\n  const cached = STATUS_CACHE.get(provider)\n  if (cached) return cached\n  ...\n  const settle = (status) => { STATUS_CACHE.set(provider, status); return status }\n  ...\n}\n```\nSimplest: wrap the body in a helper `probeProvider` and cache result:\n\n```js\nexport function checkProvider(provider, { probe = true } = {}) {\n  if (!probe) return { state: 'unverified', version: null, detail: 'probe disabled' }\n  const cached = STATUS_CACHE.get(provider)\n  if (cached) return cached\n  const status = probeProvider(provider)\n  STATUS_CACHE.set(provider, status)\n  return status\n}\n```\nwhere probeProvider contains the original body minus the probe check.\n\nCareful: the a5-shell overlay keeps shell: win32 logic; nocache overlay keeps `shell: process.platform === 'win32'` so a5-shell repro still holds in the nocache canary (irrelevant, separate).\n\nCareful: obj identity — providerStatus(config) called twice with the same config object → same provider object → cache hits. Good.\n\nWrite it.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6e5ba867444bd771672006700a3","_messageId":"01a1b6e9954