setup)`? Simpler: each test creates and removes at the end.\n\nI'll write a helper:\n\n```js\nfunction defectRoot({ repro, copySource = \"export const BROKEN = true\\n\", overlay = \"export const BROKEN = false\\n\", canary = true, edits = null }) {\n  const root = tempRoot()\n  write(root, `${COPY}lib/select.mjs`, copySource)\n  write(root, 'test/characterization/defects/mini.test.mjs', repro)\n  if (canary) {\n    const data = { defect: 'mini' }\n    if (edits) data.repro_edits = edits\n    write(root, 'test/characterization/canary/mini/canary.json', JSON.stringify(data) + '\\n')\n    if (overlay !== null) write(root, 'test/characterization/canary/mini/overlay/lib/select.mjs', overlay)\n  }\n  return root\n}\n\nfunction ledgerFor(repro, extra = {}) {\n  return { id: 'mini', owner_task: 'T-001', owner_milestone: 'M1', ac: 'AC-001', repro_sha256: reproSha256(repro), ...extra }\n}\n```\n\nFor case 13 (missing canary): `canary: false` → but then no canary.json → canary_missing. Good.\n\nFor case 14: copySource BROKEN=false, overlay BROKEN=true → baseline fails.\n\nLet me now write the test file with the 15 exact titles.\n\nTitles from design §6 (must match acceptance A-1 substrings):\n1. `[AC-005] frozen: untouched fixture root passes`\n2. `[AC-005] frozen: changing one registered byte fails with frozen.hash_mismatch`\n3. `[AC-005] frozen: CRLF checkout of a registered file still passes`\n4. `[AC-005] frozen: lib/, bin/ and config/ paths are rejected as frozen.forbidden_path`\n5. `[AC-005] frozen: scripts/ and other unlisted paths fail with frozen.outside_allowed`\n6. `[AC-005] frozen: contracts/spec and contracts/golden paths are allowed`\n7. `[AC-005] frozen: unregistered file in the v0.1 copy fails with frozen.unregistered`\n8. `[AC-005] frozen: missing registered file fails with frozen.file_missing`\n9. `[AC-005] frozen: path traversal and absolute paths are rejected`\n10. `[AC-005] defects: well-formed fixture ledger passes`\n11. `[AC-005] defects: repro edited a