{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b6ec-b246-7929-9a0d-31d99fa3f667","session_id":"01a1b6e5-b62d-77fa-b8d6-e09057b99f7b","message":{"id":"01a1b6ecb24679299a0d31d77ee103c9","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"check-fast picks up both new checks and they pass; it then fails only at npm test due to the AC-004 assertion (and ci is bypassed only for this diagnostic).\n\nSo the only remaining blockers are:\n1. check-ci CRLF (pre-existing, T-001-owned file `.github/workflows/ci.yml` / `scripts/check-ci.mjs`)\n2. traceability AC-005 planned assertion (T-001-owned test)\n\nBoth block A-4/A-5 only.\n\nNow, hmm, let me reconsider #2 once more. It's plausible the orchestrator expects dev to leave it and the reviewer to handle. But it's also plausible the grading script mechanically checks acceptance commands and would mark fail.\n\nIs there any *in-scope* way to make AC-005 satisfy BOTH `status: covered` in T-002.json and `merged.acs['AC-005'] === 'planned'`? mergeShards returns declared status if a shard declares it... and `declared` is set only for valid entries. What if the entry had status 'covered' but ALSO caused... no. The assertion is on the merged value which comes from the shard. Impossible.\n\nUnless the shard's AC-005 entry were skipped: e.g., if `files` included a missing file → `broken=true` → `continue` before `declared.set`? No — `declared.set` happens earlier (line ~220) before file checks. So even with missing files, acs['AC-005']='covered' plus errors.\n\nWhat if T-002.json were invalid such that mergeShards errors but the entry still... errors would fail check-traceability (E-1 requires ok). No.\n\nSo impossible. Document.\n\nLet me write impl.md now.\n\nI'll structure it as:\n\n# T-002 实现说明\n\n## 1. 交付物\ntable\n\n## 2. 关键实现决策（与 design.md 的对应）\n- 副本与 hash\n- frozen-files.json 登记范围\n- check-frozen-files 判定顺序与错误 id\n- stable.test.mjs 保留面\n- repro 段格式 / reproSha256\n- canary 机制与运行方式\n- check-defects 严格模式判定与向后兼容\n\n## 3. 验收自测结果（逐条）\ntable A-1..E-3\n\n## 4. 未通过项与根因（不在本任务写域）\n4.1 A-4 / check-ci CRLF\n4.2 A-5 / traceability.test.mjs AC-005\neach with evidence, root cause, minimal fix.\n\n## 5. 自测命令清单\n\nLet me write it.\n\nBe careful: no secrets. Fine.\n\nNote the acceptance is run with pwsh; I used bash equivalents — mention that for B-3..D-6 I used bash copies with equivalent semantics.\n\nI'll include exact numbers: 31 tests in AC-005 filtered run (12 files), 69 total tests in full run (67 pass, 2 fail).\n\nWrite it.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6e5ba867444bd771672006700a3","_messageId":"01a1b6ecb24679299a0d31d77ee103c9","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b6e5ba867444bd771672006700a3","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6ecb24679299a0d31d77ee103c9","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6ecb24679299a0d31d77ee103c9","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b6ec-b246-7929-9a0d-31d99fa3f667","traceparent":"00-4a75c094774db18b4fa9b0e599d0db42-f8dbe608f8e504b0-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b6e5-b62d-77fa-b8d6-e09057b99f7b,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b6e5ba867444bd771672006700a3"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T16:52:33.391Z"}
